{:edb/db-before-t 2793 :edb/db-after-t 2794 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536106 50 #inst "2026-10-09T15:07:46.084Z" 13194139536106 true] [17592186124520 1020 #edb/ref 17592186383886 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1017 #edb/ref 17592186383887 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1089 "q-37085" 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1100 "Determine if the matrix\n$A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$\nis diagonalizable or not, and if it is diagonalizable, find a corresponding diagonal matrix $D.$" 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1113 #uuid "1c3b0ba8-8f1e-5b85-96e6-708a54bce1fa" 13194139536106 true] [17592186383886 1145 "Since $A$ is triangular, the eigenvalues are the entries on the main diagonal. \n\nSo, the eigenvalues are ${\\lambda }_{1}={\\lambda }_{2}=-2.$ Since we get one repeated eigenvalue, the matrix might not be diagonalizable. To check this, we row-reduce the matrix $(A-(-2)I)\\text{x}=0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-(-2)I & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+2[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe reduced matrix above has only $1$ pivot column. This implies that we will have only $2-1=1$ linearly independent eigenvector corresponding to the current eigenvalue. Therefore, $A$ is not diagonalizable." 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383888 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383889 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383890 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383891 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1000 #edb/ref 17592186383892 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1041 "selection" 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1104 #edb/ref 17592186383892 13194139536106 true] [17592186383887 1110 #uuid "7791661f-fd1